        "original_id": "d7dfaef1-ee8d-5faf-96e3-38e5d66641bb",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jack Maitland, Alan Faneca, Darrelle Revis, Nick Mangold, Shaun Ellis, D’Brickashaw Ferguson\n- Organizations: National Football League, Pittsburgh Steelers, Seattle Seahawks, New York Jets\n- Products: Super Bowl ring, Vince Lombardi Trophy\n- Events: Super Bowl XL, 2010 Pro Bowl\n- Topics: American football honors and awards\n\nFacts:\n- John Frederick \"Jack\" Maitland was born on February 8, 1948.\n- Jack Maitland is a former American football running back who played in the National Football League in the 1970s.\n- Jack Maitland earned a Super Bowl ring.\n- The Vince Lombardi Trophy is awarded only to the winning team ownership, while the Super Bowl ring serves as a collectible memento for players and team members to keep as a symbol of victory.\n- Alan Faneca was selected six times as a first-team All-Pro and nine times for the Pro Bowl.\n- Alan Faneca won a Super Bowl ring with the Pittsburgh Steelers in Super Bowl XL by defeating the Seattle Seahawks.\n- In the 2009 New York Jets season, the New York Jets were represented at the 2010 Pro Bowl by Darrelle Revis, Nick Mangold, Shaun Ellis, D’Brickashaw Ferguson, and Alan Faneca.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
